  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem: the taskbar (Win+1–9) section of the new Shortcut Guide being cut off on the left and misaligned in 0.100.2. The closest tickets describe different problems. PowerToys#48435 covers the taskbar number indicator glitching when the taskbar isn't at the bottom of the screen. PowerToys#48773 covers a crash or mispositioned overlay when you select the Windows tab, mostly on Windows 10. This looks like a new layout bug. Please keep the ticket open and add your Windows version, display scaling (DPI) and resolution, and taskbar position and alignment. A PowerToys bug report ZIP would also help. If your taskbar isn't at the bottom, that may be related to #48435.\"}",
